1, roughly 1.5 °C in all. There is a strong, well-established El Niño effect on temperature: after El Niño conditions in the preceding fall, Mar–May tends to run cooler, and El Niño accounts for about 15% of the year-to-year ups and downs. With this year's strong El Niño, that push is about 80% of a normal year-to-year swing. Without El Niño, a Mar–May this cool would come about once every 4 years. Humidity shows no clear long-term trend, but El Niño may have an effect toward a more humid Mar–May, though the evidence is thin, and this year's shift is a noticeable tilt. Rainfall shows no clear trend or El Niño link. For Mar–May 2027, the temperature odds are close to even. The El Niño expected for Sep–Nov 2026 is stronger than any in the record used here, so the outlook extends the historical relationship beyond what has been observed. This outlook is based on the El Niño strength expected for Sep–Nov 2026 and will be updated when it is observed in early December.","variables":{"temperature":{"normal_1991_2020":20.2959,"trend_per_decade":0.1952,"trend_p":0.0002,"trend_total_since_1951":1.464,"enso_effect_per_degC":-0.4538,"enso_p":0.0002,"confidence":"Strong","survives_fdr":true,"fraction_explained":0.1711,"intrinsic_sd":0.9363,"effect_this_season":-0.7111,"effect_ratio":0.7594,"size":"Substantial","size_typical_el_nino":"Noticeable","once_every_n_years_without_el_nino":4,"expected_anomaly_2027":-0.1918,"forecast_mean":20.1042,"forecast_sd":0.9974,"p_below":0.3996,"p_near":0.2858,"p_above":0.3146,"forecast_words":"Near-equal odds of below, near and above normal","within_record":false,"enso_effect_shrunk_per_degC":-0.2811,"shrink_factor":0.6193,"effect_this_season_raw":-1.1482,"trend_part_2027":0.5193,"roni_upper_within_record":false,"years_of_warming_equivalent":-36.4277,"percentiles":{"p05":{"trend_per_decade":0.3472,"trend_p":0.0065,"enso_effect_per_degC":-0.3109,"enso_p":0.2891,"confidence":"No identifiable effect","shift_this_season":-0.7865,"lines_cross":false},